        arc:
          'She moves from a child who imagines she can fix the world to an adult who accepts that she cannot live in the country she loves. Vienna strips her of certainty, homelessness strips her of pride, and the return to Iran teaches her that she no longer fits anywhere completely. By the last pages she has stopped looking for a home and started building a life, taking her grandmother’s instruction about integrity with her instead of a nationality.',
