    aboutAuthor:
      'Paulo Coelho was born in Rio de Janeiro in 1947 and announced early that he intended to be a writer, a wish his parents met by having him confined to a psychiatric institution more than once during his teenage years. He drifted through law school, theater, and journalism, and in the 1970s he wrote lyrics for one of Brazil’s most popular rock musicians, work that brought him to the attention of the country’s military dictatorship and led to his being detained.\n\nThe turning point came in 1986, when he walked the ancient pilgrimage route to Santiago de Compostela in Spain. He wrote about that journey in his first widely read book and followed it with *The Alchemist*, published in 1988 and written, by his account, in about two weeks, because he says the story was already written in his soul. Its first Brazilian publisher gave up the rights after disappointing sales.\n\nWord of mouth then did what marketing had not. The novel became a bestseller in Brazil, was picked up internationally, and has gone on to sell in the tens of millions and be translated into dozens of languages. Coelho has published many books since, most of them concerned with faith, destiny, and self-discovery, and he has become one of the most widely read and most fiercely debated authors alive, admired by readers who credit him with changing their lives and dismissed by critics who find his wisdom too easily won.',
